1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,487
Welcome & Golden Rules.

2
00:00:02,437 --> 00:00:06,837
Foundational rules and vocabulary that keep every service safe.

3
00:00:06,837 --> 00:00:10,200
When sound is done well, nobody notices.

4
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:14,650
Our job is to help the congregation hear the message and music clearly.

5
00:00:14,650 --> 00:00:18,800
Nothing you do today can break this console if you follow the rules.

6
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:21,087
The Seven Golden Rules.

7
00:00:21,087 --> 00:00:25,012
Recall, don't save: Load the Sunday scene every week.

8
00:00:25,012 --> 00:00:28,475
Never save over it unless the sound lead asks.

9
00:00:28,475 --> 00:00:35,600
Fix the channel, not the master: If one mic is too loud or feeding back, pull that channel's fader — not the main LR.

10
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:40,837
Gain is set at sound check: Once service starts, use faders to adjust volume.

11
00:00:40,837 --> 00:00:44,012
Only change gain if the sound lead says so.

12
00:00:44,012 --> 00:00:49,925
Stay off the setup screens: No changes to routing, output, or Setup menus during service.

13
00:00:49,925 --> 00:00:55,562
Mute what isn't used: An open mic with nobody talking picks up noise and causes feedback.

14
00:00:55,562 --> 00:00:59,325
Watch and listen: Eyes on the stage, ears on the room.

15
00:00:59,325 --> 00:01:02,025
Be ready before someone speaks.

16
00:01:02,025 --> 00:01:06,962
Stay calm and ask: Mute the problem, take a breath, then call the sound lead.

17
00:01:06,962 --> 00:01:08,637
Don't guess.

18
00:01:08,637 --> 00:01:10,787
Seven Words to Know.

19
00:01:10,787 --> 00:01:15,600
Channel: One input — like one mic or instrument — with its own fader.

20
00:01:15,600 --> 00:01:19,775
Gain: How much the console boosts the mic signal coming in.

21
00:01:19,775 --> 00:01:22,200
Set once at sound check.

22
00:01:22,200 --> 00:01:26,237
Fader: The slider that sets how loud a channel is in the room.

23
00:01:26,237 --> 00:01:28,937
Mute: Silences a channel.

24
00:01:28,937 --> 00:01:33,075
A lit (red) MUTE button means the channel is OFF.

25
00:01:33,075 --> 00:01:38,237
Mix / Monitor: A separate blend sent to stage speakers or in-ear monitors.

26
00:01:38,237 --> 00:01:41,875
Scene: A saved snapshot of the whole console.

27
00:01:41,875 --> 00:01:45,012
The X32 holds up to 100.

28
00:01:45,012 --> 00:01:48,700
Feedback: The squeal when a mic picks up a speaker.

29
00:01:48,700 --> 00:01:51,612
Pull that channel's fader down quickly.

